<title>EGYPT: Egypt's BOP $577 mln in surplus in 1995/6.</title>
<headline>Egypt's BOP $577 mln in surplus in 1995/6.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt's balance of payments was $577 million in surplus in the financial year 1995/6, against a surplus of $754 million in the previous year, the central bank said in a report available on Tuesday.</p>
<p>But the current account was $125 million in deficit, compared with a surplus of $387 million in 1994/5, it added.</p>
<p>Here is a detailed balance of payments table (all figures in millions of U.S. dollars):</p>
<p>						 1995/6	1994/5</p>
<p> TRADE BALANCE			     -9,234	-7,853</p>
<p>   Exports				    4,593	 4,957</p>
<p>     Oil and products		     2,226	 2,176</p>
<p>     Non-oil exports			2,367	 2,781</p>
<p>   Imports				  -13,827     -12,810</p>
<p> BALANCE OF SERVICES		     +5,377	+4,042</p>
<p> BALANCE OF TRANSFERS		    +3,732	+4,198</p>
<p>    Official				    932	   919</p>
<p>    Private				   2,800	 3,279</p>
<p> CURRENT ACCOUNT BALANCE		   -125	  +387</p>
<p> NET CAPITAL OPERATIONS		     813	   430</p>
<p>    Direct investment in Egypt	    630	   783</p>
<p>    Direct investment abroad		-15	   -48</p>
<p>    Portfolio investment		     50	     4</p>
<p>    Other investments (net)		 148	  -309</p>
<p> ERRORS AND OMISSIONS			-111	   -63</p>
<p> OVERALL BALANCE OF PAYMENTS	     +577	  +754</p>
<p>-- Jonathan Wright +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
